{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalReebDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalReebDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Endomorphism","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.reeb_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.reeb_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L100-L100","doc":"Periodicity: `ξ_q^{Ω_q} = id_A`.  The power and identity are\ntaken in the endomorphism monoid `End obj`, whose multiplication\nis composition and whose unit `1` is `𝟙 obj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.reeb_normalizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.reeb_normalizes","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L96-L96","doc":"Normalization: `ξ_q ∘ θ = θ`, i.e. the derivation preserves the\ncontact form (`reeb ≫ contact = contact`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.period","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.period","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The period of the Reeb flow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.contact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.contact","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The contact form `θ : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.reeb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.reeb","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The Reeb derivation `ξ_q : A → A`, carried as an element of the\nendomorphism monoid `End obj` so that the periodicity field below\ncan use its monoid power.  `End obj` unfolds to `obj ⟶ obj`, so\n`reeb ≫ contact` still elaborates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.toReebAlgebraData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation.toReebAlgebraData","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L83-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CategoricalReebDerivation","kind":"structure","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L67-L100","doc":"**CategoricalReebDerivation**: a derivation `ξ_q : A → A` on a\nFrobenius–Hopf substrate, equipped with a contact form `θ` and a\nperiod `Ω_q` such that the iterated composition `ξ_q^Ω_q = id_A`.\n\nTwo of the narrative's (`def:categorical-reeb-derivation`)\nconditions are encoded as fields below:\n* **Normalization** `ξ_q ∘ θ = θ` (`reeb_normalizes`), and\n* **Periodicity** `ξ_q^{Ω_q} = id_A` (`reeb_periodic`).\n\nThe narrative's **derivation / Leibniz rule**\n`ξ_q ∘ μ = μ ∘ (ξ_q ⊗ id + id ⊗ ξ_q)` is *not* encoded as a field\nhere: its additive form `ξ_q ⊗ id + id ⊗ ξ_q` requires a\npreadditive ambient category, so it is recorded in the narrative\nonly and deferred to the preadditive specialisation.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-reeb-derivation}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-reeb-derivation","label":"def:categorical-reeb-derivation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData.unit","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Unit `η : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData.mul","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Multiplication `μ : A ⊗ A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData.obj","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The underlying object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebAlgebraData","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-derivation.lean#L39-L65","doc":"**Reeb algebra data**: the object, multiplication and unit that the\nReeb derivation below consumes, and nothing else.\n\nThis is a file-local minimal carrier, **not** a Frobenius–Hopf\nsubstrate.  It was named `FrobeniusHopfSubstrate` until 2026-09-15,\nwhich collided — at the *fully qualified* name\n`QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate` — with the canonical\neight-field structure in `frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean` and with a\nthird three-field carrier in `substrate-self-duality.lean`.  Nothing\nimported two of the three, so the collision was latent rather than a\nbuild error; renamed per bean `qou-hmhw`.\n\nWhat it is NOT, and the difference is load-bearing: it carries no\ncomultiplication, no counit, no antipode, no Frobenius form and no\nlaws.  In particular the antipode axioms added to the canonical\nstructure on 2026-09-14 (bean `qou-c64q`) do not apply here, so a\nreader must not transport results about that structure to this one.\n\nRef: [kock2004] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443 ","signatureChunk":0}]}